  "id": "DrugBank_DB01112 - MONDO_4471",
  "verbalization": "Cefuroxime is implicated in the pathogenesis of bacterial arthritis through a chain of indications that ultimately converge on this condition. The drug is linked to Streptococcal Meningitis, Acute Gonococcal Endometritis, and Gonorrhea, all of which are associated with Cefoxitin, a related antibiotic. Cefoxitin, in turn, is indicated for bacterial arthritis, suggesting a potential pathway where Cefuroxime may contribute to the development of this condition through its antibacterial activity. The evidence suggests that Cefuroxime could be a contributing factor in the treatment or prevention of bacterial arthritis, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cefuroxime in the broader context of antibiotic use and its potential impact on bacterial infections, particularly in cases where the causative pathogens are sensitive to the drug.",
